About THIA

THIA is transforming how small and medium enterprises build internal applications and automate business processes. Our AI powered platform enables business experts to create custom applications using natural language eliminating the need for expensive development teams. We're well funded, generating revenue, and solving real problems for companies that need more than off the shelf software.

About the Role

We’re looking for an IT & Compliance Engineer to own the day to day IT operations and some compliance execution that keeps our infrastructure running and our users and devices audit ready. You’ll work directly alongside the Director of IT & Security, allowing you to go deep on server infrastructure, systems administration, device and user management, and compliance program management.

This is a hands-on, high ownership role on a small, senior team. You’ll have real responsibility from day one and direct input into how we run and scale our IT environment as the company grows.

What You’ll Do

Systems Administration

Perform Linux server administration including resource optimization, log analysis, system updates, and service recovery
Support and maintain cross cloud backup strategies, including self hosted AWS backup configurations
Manage service accounts, and IAM access across applications.
Device & User Management

Support endpoint management across Windows, macOS, and Linux using JumpCloud MDM provisioning, policy enforcement, and full device lifecycle
Ensure all managed devices are enrolled, compliant, and reporting correctly across MDM and security tooling
Deploy and maintain endpoint agents (EDR, DLP, monitoring) across the device fleet and verify agent health
Manage user accounts, SSO, MFA, and RBAC across business applications
Own the onboarding and offboarding process end-to-end provisioning access, issuing devices, deprovisioning accounts, and ensuring clean offboarding audit trails
Enforce and verify device compliance posture, disk encryption, password policies, OS patching, and screen lock ensuring every device passes compliance checks.
Handle IT management, device setup, and hardware lifecycle management
Provide internal IT support and act as the first escalation point for technical issues
Compliance & Audit Management

Manage the CMMC Level 2 compliance program end-to-end, gap tracking, evidence collection, POA&M management, and audit readiness
Maintain SOC 2 and ISO 27001 compliance activities, including control evidence, test scheduling, and remediation follow through
Ensure all devices and users remain in compliance across device monitoring checks, resolving failures, and maintaining clean audit evidence
Track and close compliance and remediation tickets in Jira
Maintain policy documentation, runbooks, and internal IT management procedures in Confluence
What We’re Looking For

Must-Haves

Due to U.S. Government contract requirements, this position is open only to U.S. citizens.

3+ years of experience in an IT operations, systems administration, cloud infrastructure, IT generalist role, or equivalent demonstrated depth
Scripting experience in Bash or PowerShell for automating routine IT and infrastructure tasks
Linux administration experience: comfortable on the command line, managing services, logs, and system configuration
Experience managing endpoints and users via an MDM platform (JumpCloud, Intune, or similar)
Experience administering SaaS applications, SSO integrations, and identity management
Demonstrated management of device and user compliance: ensuring endpoints meet policy requirements and pass audit checks
Experience supporting one or more compliance program: SOC 2, ISO 27001, CMMC, NIST 800-171, or similar
Strong documentation habits: able to write clear runbooks, policies, and audit evidence
Eligibility and willingness to serve as Facility Security Officer (FSO) for CMMC Level 2, including any required training or certification
Highly organized, self-directed, and comfortable managing multiple workstreams without heavy oversight
Nice to Have

Exposure to security tooling at an operational level
Prior experience as an FSO or in a DoD/federal contracting compliance role
Familiarity with Jira administration
Direct experience with Secureframe, Vanta or a comparable GRC platform
Familiarity with CMMC Level 2 assessment process and CUI handling requirements
Background in a startup or fast moving environment where you’ve had to build as well as operate
